;; `boring.records` requires `boring.core` for the `boring/` alias used inside
;; a macro's syntax quote, which resolves at EXPANSION time. clj-kondo cannot
;; see that through a reader conditional and reports the require as unused.
;;
;; Scoped with `:config-in-ns` rather than excluded globally: an unused require
;; of `boring.core` anywhere else is still a real finding worth hearing about.
;;
;; Not an inline `#_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-namespace]}`, which suppressed
;; the warning and was then itself reported as `Redundant ignore` at every
;; placement tried.
{:config-in-ns {boring.records {:linters {:unused-namespace {:level :off}}}}}
